# L §2.5 (round 12) at a fulfils: pay is keyed by n in 1 .. cnt (cnt = 3), so pay[2] names an instance; a statement
# covering konto in January books the observation (12.00 PLN) and leaves the other two instances open (L §5.19
# Coverage): konto 100 - 12 = 88.00 PLN; observed(pay[2]) is the observation's leg (pay[5], no value of 1 .. 3, is
# L2_5_stepped_range_fulfils_out.test). (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §2.5, writer 5's T-4.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input cnt: int
input first_day: date
input bank: observed

move pay[n in 1 .. cnt]: transfers
  on add_days(first_day, n)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "s"
  cnt = 3 "s"
  first_day = 2026-01-01 "s"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-01
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-01-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 12.00 PLN, fulfils: pay[2]) "l1"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31), observed(pay[2]).cash.amount
=== expect
q: (88.00 PLN, 12.00 PLN)
  open: pay[1]
  open: pay[3]
  cut 2026-12-31
